# ${name}

[中文](README.md) | [English](README.en.md)

A pnpm monorepo layout template. The backend is built on [@axiosleo/koapp](https://github.com/AxiosLeo/node-koapp) and ships a Session-authenticated admin API, a multi-app / Api-Key skeleton, and an empty `/openapi` surface for your business modules.

## Features

- **Two API surfaces**: `/api/*` (Session cookie) and `/openapi/*` (Bearer Api-Key)
- **Admin console**: login, plus app and Api-Key CRUD
- **Multi-app Api-Keys**: tokens use the `sk2a_` prefix; plaintext is shown only once at creation
- **SQLite metadata**: apps and keys live in an internal DB (default `./data/${name}.db`)
- **CLI**: manage apps and keys via `${name} app` / `${name} apikey`
- **Health check**: `GET /api/health` (no auth)

## Requirements

- Node.js `>= 20`
- pnpm `>= 9`

## Quick start

```bash
# Install dependencies
pnpm install

# Configure env (login is disabled while ADMIN_PASSWORD is empty)
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env and set at least ADMIN_PASSWORD

# Start the API in dev mode (default 0.0.0.0:8082)
pnpm --filter ${name}-services run dev
```

Verify the service:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/health
```

## Directory layout

```
.
├── apps/
│   └── services/          # Backend API (@axiosleo/koapp)
│       └── src/
│           ├── modules/   # admin, app, …
│           ├── middlewares/
│           └── services/  # SQLite metadata
├── packages/
│   ├── commands/          # CLI command implementations (app / apikey)
│   └── utils/             # Shared utils placeholder
├── .agents/               # Agent rules and koapp skill docs
├── .env.example
└── package.json           # Workspace root (bin: ${name})
```

## Architecture and auth

```
Client ──Session cookie──► /api/*        ──► admin login (public)
                                         ──► apps / keys CRUD (authenticated)
Client ──Bearer sk2a_…──► /openapi/*     ──► business routers (skeleton, Api-Key required)
                              │
                              ▼
                     SQLite (apps / api_keys)
```

| Surface | Auth | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/api/*` | Session cookie | Admin console: login, apps, and key management |
| `/openapi/*` | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` | External business API; template mounts auth middleware and a 404 fallback only |

## Admin API (Session)

Public routes:

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/api/login` | Login, body: `{ username, password }` |
| `GET` | `/api/logout` | Logout |
| `GET` | `/api/profile` | Current user (requires session) |
| `GET` | `/api/health` | Health check (no auth) |

After login:

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/api/apps` | Create app |
| `GET` | `/api/apps` | List apps |
| `GET` | `/api/apps/{:id}` | App detail |
| `PATCH` | `/api/apps/{:id}` | Update app |
| `DELETE` | `/api/apps/{:id}` | Delete app |
| `GET` | `/api/apps/{:id}/keys` | List Api-Keys |
| `POST` | `/api/apps/{:id}/keys` | Create Api-Key (plaintext returned once) |
| `DELETE` | `/api/apps/{:id}/keys/{:keyId}` | Revoke Api-Key |

## OpenAPI surface (Api-Key)

Request header:

```http
Authorization: Bearer sk2a_<40 hex chars>
```

- Keys are stored as SHA-256 hashes; the plaintext printed at creation is never shown again
- Both the app and the key must be `active`
- Mount business routers under the `/openapi` `root` Router in [`apps/services/src/modules/index.ts`](apps/services/src/modules/index.ts)

## CLI

Command implementations live in `packages/commands/`. Build services first, and ensure the root package entry `bin/${name}.js` is available:

```bash
pnpm --filter ${name}-services run build
```

Apps:

```bash
${name} app create --name my-app [--desc "..."]
${name} app list
${name} app remove --name my-app --yes
```

Api-Keys:

```bash
${name} apikey create --app <app_id> [--name default]
${name} apikey list --app <app_id>
${name} apikey revoke --id <key_id>
```

The CLI loads the monorepo root `.env` (for example `SQLITE_PATH`) so it shares the same metadata DB as the API process.

